### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a card that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that gives perspective */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Creates 3D space */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;    /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover state – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front & Back faces */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;     /* Hide backside when rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

.card-front {
  background: #f9f9f9;
}

.card-back {
  background: #e0e0e0;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);      /* Flip back face so it's readable after rotation */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      <p>Front Content</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      <p>Back Content</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective (`perspective: 1000px`). |
| `.card` | Holds the two faces, has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so child elements keep their 3D positioning. |
| `.card:hover` | Applies a 180° Y‑rotation on hover. |
| `.card-face` | Common styling for both sides. |
| `.card-front` | Normal front face. |
| `.card-back` | Rotated 180° so that when the card flips, this side becomes visible. |

Feel free to replace the text with images or other content. Adjust the `perspective`, `transition`, and colors to fit your design.
